---
title: ":chocolate_bar: Old-Fashioned Fudge"
source: Recipe Box
servings: 16
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
total time: 2 hours
tags:
  - desserts
  - chocolate
  - candy
  - fudge
  - recipe-box
  - vegetarian
---

Butter a #loaf pan{}.

In a #2-qt saucepan{}, mix @sugar{2%cups}, @milk{2/3%cup}, @unsweetened chocolate{2%oz}, @corn syrup{2%Tbsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp}.

Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, until chocolate is melted and sugar is dissolved.

Cook, stirring occasionally, until reaching 234°F on a #candy thermometer{}.

Remove from heat; add @butter{2%Tbsp}. Cool mixture to 120°F without stirring.

Add @vanilla extract{1%tsp}; beat vigorously for 5 to ~{10%minutes} until candy is thick and no longer glossy.

Quickly stir in coarsely chopped @nuts{1/2%cup}.

Spread mixture evenly in the prepared loaf pan. Cool until firm, then cut into 1-inch squares.
